content:
After materials are sorted, the completed field work is checked in to MOJO. Refer to Figure 20 for an explanation of the overall check-in process.
Figure 20. Overview of office check-in procedures for production.
![](/images/imports/1/image1_ddc1b69f.png){width="6.333333333333333in" height="8.34375in"}

FRs use the SC-921, *Add Page* to record GQ addresses found while canvassing in their Assignment Area. The Add Page is used to add both new HUs, GQs and TLs. The SCS will review and approve all address adds. After approval of any of the GQ adds, they are then included in the GQAC workload to make an enumeration appointment and enter the GQ into MOJO. Refer to the SC-445, for procedures on how to enter an added GQ in MOJO.
The SC-921, *Add Page* have designated fields for the FRs to input information found in the field. It is important that these fields are completed accurately to ensure that address verification can occur in the office. FRs will number each SC-921, *Add Page* using the Page \_\_\_ of \_\_\_ spaces in the upper right corner. The pages are to be numbered one after the other using the first blank space. For example, if an FR has 3 sheets of Add Pages, the FR will complete each like this:
Page [1]{.underline} of [3]{.underline}
Page [2]{.underline} of [3]{.underline}
Page [3]{.underline} of [3]{.underline}
The following image is an example of the SC-921, Add Page.
![](/images/imports/1/image3_1abacb97.png){width="6.5in" height="3.875in"}

The Header contains the address and geographic codes information about the GQ.
![Image showing the header section of the SC-116, Group Quarters Control Record. No data has been entered into this form.](/images/imports/1/image3_1abacb97.png){width="5.9994695975503065in" height="4.966227034120735in"}
The clerk confirms that the address information is still correct during the interview with the GQ Contact Person. Each header will have a unique Barcode ID for each *Special Census Group Quarters Control Record*. The information in items A through Q is printed on the form.

Print the Form SC-117 from MOJO and staple the pages together in the upper left-hand corner. Make certain that the pages are in the correct order.
The Header information and the TL contact name and telephone number (if available), in Section A, *Transitory Location Facility Contact Information* of the Form SC-117, will be prepopulated from the record in MOJO to the form. The following image is an example of Form SC-117.
![Image showing an example of the SC-117, Transitory Location Control Record. The form is blank.](/images/imports/1/image4_5a3fa4b0.jpeg){width="4.116367016622922in" height="4.7264381014873145in"}

## Overview
The Field Supervisor performs an initial observation of each Field Representative within one week after the Field Representative receives their first assignment. The Field Supervisor uses Form SC-1222, Special Census Observation Checklist, to observe the Field Representative in the field. Results from the observation are keyed into MOJO by office clerks. The following images provide examples of the front and back of the SC-1222, Special Census Observation Checklist.
![Image showing an example of the first page of the Form SC-1222, Special Census Observation Checklist. ](/images/imports/1/image5_9a76b513.png){width="6.44in" height="8.17in"}
![Image showing an example of the second page of the Form SC-1222, Special Census Observation Checklist. ](/images/imports/1/image6_98eef807.png){width="6.47in" height="8.2in"}

## Filtering Tables
There are three methods to search by attributes in most tables.
1. Filters above the table for specific data attributes. These filters may allow the user to select one or more value for that attribute. The selections you make filter the results table appropriately.
![](/images/imports/1/image7_e63915e1.png){width="1.0212871828521435in" height="1.7860640857392827in"}
60. Many tables include search boxes about the table for specific data attributes. These allow the user to search on a string value for that attribute and will filter the results table appropriately.
![](/images/imports/1/image7_e63915e1.png){width="3.054280402449694in" height="0.42402121609798776in"}
61. Most columns in the tables are filterable by text. The user can simply type a character string in the column filter box (under the column name) and that column will be filtered by that character value.
![](/images/imports/1/image7_e63915e1.png){width="4.431667760279965in" height="0.8721292650918635in"}

Many of the tables also have a map component. Depending on which screen the user is on, the map may plot staff, cases, and/or geographic boundaries. The user can view either the table of results, map of results, or both at the same time.
![](/images/imports/1/image7_e63915e1.png){width="6.5in" height="2.0027777777777778in"}
1. To view only the table of results, select the table icon on the slider bar ![](/images/imports/1/image7_e63915e1.png){width="0.26591207349081364in" height="0.35976377952755906in"}
62. To view only the map of results, select the map icon on the slider bar ![](/images/imports/1/image7_e63915e1.png){width="0.2767760279965004in" height="0.35585520559930006in"}
